  "notes": "Astarta Holding N.V. (Warsaw GPW, EUR reporting). Largest Ukrainian sugar producer + soybean processor + farming + cattle. ~220,000 ha land bank under lease/use (~543k acres). Quarterly reporter. Segments: Sugar (largest in normal years), Soybean Processing, Farming (crops: corn, sunflower, wheat, soybeans), Cattle Farming. War-impacted from Q1 2022; some assets in occupied territories written down 2022. Hectares converted via × 2.47. EUR figures from published quarterly press releases / annual reports. Astarta IPO'd on Warsaw GPW in August 2006 (one of the first Ukrainian agri listings in Europe); land bank grew from ~37,000 ha at IPO to ~220,000 ha (2014 peak). Sugar segment built via 8 sugar plant acquisitions 2008-2012. Soybean processing plant (Globyne) commissioned 2014. Pre-2010 only annual figures available; quarterly cadence consistent from 2011. Operating expense breakdown (Cost of sales / Administrative expenses / Selling expenses / Other operating expenses) drawn from consolidated income statement of Astarta annual reports filed on astartaholding.com IR archive; quarterly press-release snapshots summarize EBITDA only, so field omitted on the Q periods.",
